WEBVTT

00:00:01.950 --> 00:00:07.890
Today on Sailor Moon, Rey not only organizes the Autumn Festival, but is its number one star.

00:00:07.890 --> 00:00:15.970
But her moment in the spotlight is cut short when a monster from the Negaverse makes a guest appearance determined to bring down the curtains.

00:00:16.770 --> 00:00:18.930
Can the Sailor Scout save the day?

00:00:19.420 --> 00:00:20.600
We'll show you.

00:02:12.570 --> 00:02:15.910
Oh, she's been at school till dinner time each night

00:02:16.010 --> 00:02:17.850
organizing the Autumn Festival.

00:02:17.950 --> 00:02:19.890
Maybe you should go see her there.

00:02:19.990 --> 00:02:22.040
Yeah, great idea.

00:02:22.140 --> 00:02:25.240
Maybe she can give us a sneak preview.

00:02:32.430 --> 00:02:33.470
- Excuse me, Ray.

00:02:33.470 --> 00:02:34.650
- What is it?

00:02:34.650 --> 00:02:37.810
- Um, we're not quite sure what to do with our class booth.

00:02:37.810 --> 00:02:40.230
- Weren't you there yesterday when I explained what to do?

00:02:40.230 --> 00:02:42.350
Do I have to explain the whole thing again?

00:02:42.350 --> 00:02:46.280
I've got my hands full, organized presentation.

00:02:46.280 --> 00:02:48.800
- Yeah, I know, but we've still got some questions

00:02:48.800 --> 00:02:50.460
we'd like to ask you about.

00:02:50.460 --> 00:02:53.530
- Okay, okay, I'll come and help you later.

00:02:53.530 --> 00:02:54.530
- What's this?

00:02:54.530 --> 00:02:56.370
What's the sound equipment doing sitting here?

00:02:56.370 --> 00:02:57.660
It should already be set up.

00:02:57.660 --> 00:02:59.300
- Ray's really something, isn't she?

00:02:59.300 --> 00:03:00.000
- Sure is.

00:03:00.670 --> 00:03:04.170
Yeah, the festival's gonna be really cool this year thanks to her.

00:03:04.170 --> 00:03:05.610
What an organizer.

00:03:05.610 --> 00:03:07.710
Hey, you two, stop dabbing and start working.

00:03:07.710 --> 00:03:08.750
We're running out of time.

00:03:08.750 --> 00:03:10.060
Right.

00:03:10.060 --> 00:03:12.560
Yeah, she's really totally the best, isn't she?

00:03:12.560 --> 00:03:13.570
For sure.

00:03:13.570 --> 00:03:14.920
Oh.

00:03:14.920 --> 00:03:15.920
Hopeless.

00:03:15.920 --> 00:03:17.560
Am I supposed to do this all myself?

00:03:17.560 --> 00:03:19.240
A cat would be more helpful.

00:03:19.240 --> 00:03:20.560
Hey, Ray.

00:03:20.560 --> 00:03:21.150
Huh?

00:03:21.150 --> 00:03:22.910
Oh, hi, Serena.

00:03:22.910 --> 00:03:25.250
Artemis and Luna at your service.

00:03:25.250 --> 00:03:26.750
What are you going on about, Serena?

00:03:26.750 --> 00:03:28.320
Can't you see I'm busy?

00:03:28.320 --> 00:03:30.000
Oh, you said a cat would be more helpful.

00:03:30.000 --> 00:03:32.720
Here, these are goodies Lita made for you.

00:03:32.720 --> 00:03:34.050
Oh, thanks.

00:03:34.050 --> 00:03:35.800
Hey, Ray, could we have a look around?

00:03:35.800 --> 00:03:36.800
Oh, sure.

00:03:36.800 --> 00:03:39.120
We're just about to have rehearsal anyway.

00:03:39.120 --> 00:03:53.170
Ray?

00:03:53.170 --> 00:03:56.200
Oh, sure, Ray, but what does cabaret lighting look like?

00:03:56.200 --> 00:03:58.250
Oh, forget it.

00:03:58.250 --> 00:04:00.000
Take a five-minute break.

00:04:03.200 --> 00:04:05.200
I practically have to do everything myself.

00:04:05.200 --> 00:04:08.200
Yeah, Ray, but that song was sounding really hot.

00:04:08.200 --> 00:04:09.200
Who wrote it anyway?

00:04:09.200 --> 00:04:11.200
Wow, you really like it, Serena?

00:04:11.200 --> 00:04:13.200
Actually, if you really want to know,

00:04:13.200 --> 00:04:16.060
I wrote all the songs for the talent show.

00:04:17.060 --> 00:04:20.090
What's wrong?

00:04:20.090 --> 00:04:23.090
You guys don't believe I'm capable of writing music?

00:04:23.090 --> 00:04:25.090
Oh, sure, Ray, we believe you.

00:04:25.090 --> 00:04:27.940
Aren't you worried it'll look like you're using this festival

00:04:27.940 --> 00:04:29.950
just to promote yourself?

00:04:31.600 --> 00:04:33.600
I'm the hardest worker here, and if it wasn't for me,

00:04:33.600 --> 00:04:35.600
there'd be no talent show.

00:04:35.600 --> 00:04:37.600
She sure doesn't suffer from low self-esteem.

00:04:37.600 --> 00:04:39.600
Hey, you can say that again.

00:04:39.600 --> 00:04:46.800
Dumb pageant.

00:04:46.800 --> 00:04:49.720
Yeah, but there should be lots of energy for us to feast on.

00:04:49.720 --> 00:04:52.900
My mouth is watering already.

00:04:52.900 --> 00:04:54.330
Right.

00:04:54.330 --> 00:04:58.290
Let's hope the dune tree likes this energy as much as you do.

00:05:00.000 --> 00:05:02.560
You ready for the big day tomorrow, Ray?

00:05:02.560 --> 00:05:05.960
You know, I just can't wait to catch your big singing debut.

00:05:05.960 --> 00:05:06.520
Great.

00:05:06.520 --> 00:05:08.220
I'm so glad Grandpa's going to make it.

00:05:08.220 --> 00:05:12.450
Yeah, Chad said he'd stay and take care of the temple.

00:05:12.450 --> 00:05:14.450
Hey, you know, Ray, I'm really impressed

00:05:14.450 --> 00:05:15.990
you wrote all those songs by yourself.

00:05:15.990 --> 00:05:18.270
Yeah, it's great, but it must have taken ages to do it.

00:05:18.270 --> 00:05:20.880
No, not at all.

00:05:20.880 --> 00:05:23.760
I came up with the lyrics first, and that didn't take too long,

00:05:23.760 --> 00:05:26.630
because you know what an ace I am at poetry.

00:05:26.630 --> 00:05:30.000
And then I worked out all the melodies, which was super fun,

00:05:30.350 --> 00:05:34.910
super cinchy. I have a knack for it.

00:05:34.910 --> 00:05:36.230
I mean, I could do it in my sleep.

00:05:40.520 --> 00:05:46.580
I gotta say, the whole thing was a snap.

00:05:46.920 --> 00:05:48.840
Must be my raw talent. Well, that's

00:05:48.840 --> 00:05:50.520
way cool, Ray. Uh,

00:05:50.680 --> 00:05:52.740
why do I have the feeling there's something

00:05:52.740 --> 00:05:54.500
very bogus about Ray's story?

00:05:54.600 --> 00:05:56.260
She's a genius or a liar.

00:05:56.260 --> 00:05:56.880
Oh,

00:06:00.350 --> 00:06:01.950
This must be the place.

00:06:02.050 --> 00:06:06.050
Ladies, you look like honest, hardworking girls.

00:06:06.150 --> 00:06:08.850
I need two girls like you to work at my temple.

00:06:08.950 --> 00:06:10.890
I'm sorry, but I'm afraid our schoolwork

00:06:10.990 --> 00:06:13.290
doesn't leave us enough time to take jobs.

00:06:13.390 --> 00:06:14.470
Thanks anyway.

00:06:14.570 --> 00:06:15.650
Goodbye.

00:06:15.750 --> 00:06:17.650
Have a nice day now.

00:06:17.750 --> 00:06:21.350
Oh, I'm sure they have lots of time for rollerblading and, boy--

00:06:21.450 --> 00:06:24.610
So where's all the bodacious food Ray told us about?

00:06:24.710 --> 00:06:25.510
I'm starving.

00:06:25.610 --> 00:06:26.420
Hang on.

00:06:26.520 --> 00:06:27.420
Where's Amy?

00:06:27.520 --> 00:06:28.260
Hey, where else?

00:06:28.360 --> 00:06:30.000
The chemistry and biology building.

00:06:30.000 --> 00:06:31.900
Say please!

00:07:00.380 --> 00:07:07.780
Worked perfectly well, don't you think?

00:07:07.780 --> 00:07:09.780
Yeah, looks like he's just the right size.

00:07:09.780 --> 00:07:10.780
Better take measurements, to be sure.

00:07:10.780 --> 00:07:11.780
Right.

00:07:11.780 --> 00:07:13.780
Uh, what is this?

00:07:13.780 --> 00:07:17.270
Could you raise your arms, please?

00:07:17.270 --> 00:07:18.260
Huh?

00:07:18.260 --> 00:07:22.210
Your arms up, just like mine are, OK?

00:07:22.210 --> 00:07:24.350
Oh, like this?

00:07:24.350 --> 00:07:25.350
That's it.

00:07:25.350 --> 00:07:27.270
Now, could you bend down, please?

00:07:27.270 --> 00:07:28.270
Oh, but I--

00:07:28.270 --> 00:07:30.000
Just take a second, see?

00:07:32.650 --> 00:07:35.090
You're absolutely perfect.

00:07:35.190 --> 00:07:37.430
We've got a perfect match over here, too.

00:07:37.530 --> 00:07:39.910
And you guys thought we were in major trouble,

00:07:40.010 --> 00:07:41.610
so come on, we'd better hurry.

00:07:41.710 --> 00:07:42.610
Wait up.

00:07:42.710 --> 00:07:44.310
Who are you people anyway?

00:07:44.410 --> 00:07:46.320
Oh, I've been rude, haven't I?

00:07:46.420 --> 00:07:49.620
My name is Sarah Howe, and I'm president of the Fashion Design

00:07:49.720 --> 00:07:50.360
Club.

00:07:50.460 --> 00:07:51.540
Our models came down with the flu,

00:07:51.640 --> 00:07:53.960
so we don't have anybody to model our designs.

00:07:54.060 --> 00:07:55.900
Would you guys mind helping us out?

00:07:56.000 --> 00:07:57.100
Models?

00:07:57.200 --> 00:08:00.000
Yeah, the theme this year is aliens from a dream.

00:08:00.410 --> 00:08:06.250
Oh, how'd this twit figure out who we really are?

00:08:06.250 --> 00:08:08.520
She must have special powers.

00:08:08.520 --> 00:08:10.340
Hey, you don't look so hot.

00:08:10.340 --> 00:08:11.190
Are you okay?

00:08:11.190 --> 00:08:12.190
What's the matter?

00:08:12.190 --> 00:08:13.190
Oh, I got it now.

00:08:13.190 --> 00:08:19.940
You're one of those people who believe in little green men with antennae and weird colored hair, aren't you?

00:08:19.940 --> 00:08:20.940
Huh?

00:08:20.940 --> 00:08:22.940
Oh, of course not.

00:08:22.940 --> 00:08:24.940
Come on, let's go.

00:08:24.940 --> 00:08:26.760
What do you want?

00:08:26.760 --> 00:08:29.090
The whole thing you want?

00:08:38.890 --> 00:08:41.110
She sure got some promotion machine, huh?

00:08:41.110 --> 00:08:43.390
Uh, Rey's never been short on self-confidence,

00:08:43.390 --> 00:08:45.760
but she sure has worked her heart out on this.

00:08:45.760 --> 00:08:48.050
Yeah, Rey's definitely got charisma.

00:08:48.050 --> 00:08:51.430
Yes, even though she's a shameless self-promoter.

00:08:51.430 --> 00:08:53.930
We better hurry, guys, or there aren't going to be any seats left.

00:08:53.930 --> 00:08:56.470
Yeah, let's book it.

00:09:01.820 --> 00:09:03.320
It's almost time to go on.

00:09:04.680 --> 00:09:07.380
You mean we gotta go out there in this?

00:09:07.480 --> 00:09:09.040
Sure, it's a fashion show.

00:09:09.410 --> 00:09:11.030
They're gonna love you out there.

00:09:11.490 --> 00:09:12.910
F-fashion show?

00:09:13.820 --> 00:09:14.560
No way!

00:09:15.350 --> 00:09:16.650
All right, you're on!

00:09:16.650 --> 00:09:19.270
Oh, oh, oh, oh, oh, oh, oh.

00:09:19.270 --> 00:09:28.630
This is embarrassing.

00:09:34.990 --> 00:09:38.070
Hey guys, isn't that Anne and Alan up there?

00:09:38.070 --> 00:09:41.740
You're right! They're sure being super cool about this.

00:09:41.740 --> 00:09:48.290
Hmm, this crowd's energy is almost at its peak.

00:09:48.290 --> 00:09:51.590
I know, and here we are ready and waiting to collect it all.

00:09:51.590 --> 00:09:55.090
It's perfect, maybe the most energy we've collected ever.

00:09:55.090 --> 00:09:58.800
If they like this, they'll be rolling in the aisles when they see our next act.

00:10:02.970 --> 00:10:08.330
They like aliens, we'll give 'em a-

00:10:08.330 --> 00:10:15.550
Gentlemen, this festival's such a big success, our very own Ray Hino!

00:10:15.550 --> 00:10:17.250
Yay!

00:10:17.250 --> 00:10:20.310
Turn!

00:10:20.310 --> 00:10:22.080
No fucking speech fright!

00:10:22.080 --> 00:10:24.660
That's not possible, you're not the one on stage!

00:10:24.660 --> 00:10:26.280
Hmm, oh, that's right!

00:10:26.280 --> 00:10:27.810
Riot, it's starting!

00:10:44.300 --> 00:10:47.100
And cuz you're so great, I wrote these special songs just for you.

00:10:47.220 --> 00:10:48.580
Now, why don't you say we get started?

00:10:49.760 --> 00:10:50.600
Oh, boy.

00:10:50.860 --> 00:10:52.380
She thinks she's a teen idol.

00:10:53.010 --> 00:10:54.290
Way to go, Ray!

00:10:55.770 --> 00:10:57.880
Won as much as I liked writing it.

00:11:07.610 --> 00:11:19.460
Pick us a Cardian to collect all that energy.

00:11:19.460 --> 00:11:22.660
Forth now!

00:12:10.490 --> 00:12:12.490
Things seem to be going just fine.

00:12:12.490 --> 00:12:15.110
Let's make our exit and wait by the Doomtree, shall we?

00:12:19.320 --> 00:12:20.550
TOG!

00:14:30.030 --> 00:14:31.910
She's sucking all my strength!

00:14:32.350 --> 00:14:49.350
Strong enough?

00:15:39.280 --> 00:15:50.900
- It's up to you.

00:15:50.900 --> 00:15:52.560
- Corner of the vast universe,

00:15:52.560 --> 00:15:55.220
there is a planet which plays a beautiful melody.

00:15:55.220 --> 00:15:57.870
It's called Planet Earth.

00:15:57.870 --> 00:15:59.480
I, the Moonlight Knight.

00:16:00.000 --> 00:16:03.780
I have vowed to never let anyone destroy its eternal song.

00:16:03.780 --> 00:16:08.900
Let music and romance live on forever.

00:16:08.900 --> 00:16:13.550
Moonlight Knight!

00:16:13.550 --> 00:16:19.360
Sailor Mars, I want to hear your beautiful voice sing from your heart once more.

00:16:19.360 --> 00:16:21.990
Thank you, Moonlight Knight!

00:17:32.680 --> 00:17:37.860
has her full powers back again.

00:17:37.860 --> 00:17:42.220
- We've all got their energy back.

00:17:42.220 --> 00:17:44.280
- I sure will.

00:18:29.500 --> 00:18:30.000
Done, Sam.

00:18:30.000 --> 00:18:34.960
Sailor Scouts, keep a melody in your heart and a lilt in your voice.

00:18:35.810 --> 00:18:36.370
So long.

00:18:37.010 --> 00:18:40.480
Oh, hunkmeister.

00:18:43.180 --> 00:18:55.170
In the universe, there is a planet which plays a beautiful melody, the planet Earth.

00:18:56.080 --> 00:19:00.000
My last song for tonight is called Starry Night.

00:19:31.210 --> 00:19:37.720
like a dream and can I tell him why

00:20:17.240 --> 00:20:24.780
I was also thinking, you're really a hard worker, aren't you, Ray?

00:20:26.860 --> 00:20:30.000
You know, it wouldn't hurt you to give it a try in one of the other.

00:20:30.990 --> 00:20:32.490
And what's that supposed to mean?

00:20:32.490 --> 00:20:35.470
That you're a lazy doughnut snorting couch potato.

00:20:35.470 --> 00:20:48.820
I take back everything I said!

00:20:48.820 --> 00:20:51.820
Standing up on that stage singing her songs in front of all those people.

00:20:51.820 --> 00:20:53.820
But not everyone is that confident.

00:20:53.820 --> 00:20:58.530
For some people, speaking up in front of classmates or even their friends can be really uncomfortable.

00:20:58.530 --> 00:21:00.000
But there's nothing wrong with being shy.

00:21:00.700 --> 00:21:02.960
If you know someone like that, encourage them.

00:21:02.960 --> 00:21:05.520
Ask them what they think and give them time to answer.

00:21:05.520 --> 00:21:06.940
They need your support.

00:21:06.940 --> 00:21:09.980
And if you're shy, know you're not the only one.

00:21:09.980 --> 00:21:11.580
The world needs all kinds of people,

00:21:11.580 --> 00:21:14.280
including shy people, Sailor Moon says.
